      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start, but it feels a bit surface-level. could u go deeper on the libertarian side? i'm looking for more than just \"rights-based frameworks\"—i want to see how they handle the idea of \"coercion\" and the moral legitimacy of the state in a more complex way. like, if they argue against taxation, what is their actual philosophical justification for why it's fundamentally immoral rather than just inefficient? try to give me the most rigorous version of their case possible.",
